f the largest clergy abuse settlements in the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Tinubu launches reelection bid amid economic woes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f902d686aae2b3f6aad3d4f2e5f86cf09508a9c34ae26d97a69662c93106eb25</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:58:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T23:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-tinubu-launches-reelection-bid-amid-economic-woes/a-79753063--a627d82d207b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-tinubu-launches-reelection-bid-amid-economic-woes/a-79753063?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Bola Tinubu promised "a better tomorrow" for Nigerians while kicking off his next electoral campaign, while also blaming his rivals for poverty plaguing Africa's most populous nation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Starlink satellite speeds restored to normal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1fd121cb1547e8107535a2082c29d77a6c9a17d8d319dd75d2b09864fd47584</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:58:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T19:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-starlink-satellite-speeds-restored-to-normal/a-79752155--bc405a2647f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-starlink-satellite-speeds-restored-to-normal/a-79752155?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The announcement comes after Starlink and Starshield restrictions had disrupted military operations in Ukraine and sparked tensions with the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German national facing trial for alleged attempt to join IS</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51a6c8170f6e334e107a32ca2b053385f6a323cdf7d4ce0563c7c1decc5d419a</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-national-facing-trial-for-alleged-attempt-to-join-is/a-79751032--cd661b98dd30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-national-facing-trial-for-alleged-attempt-to-join-is/a-79751032?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 21-year-old suspect is being held in pre-trial detention for allegedly trying to join the "Islamic State" terror group.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's new deal on Mediterranean maritime boundaries with Libya is exacerbating issues with Greece and the EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5b336f7d5867547bf4897660e70bf56d454237f5c5874a7c3247500114cf0f5</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece/a-79745971--8e4f859a6229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece-and-the-eu/a-79745971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Libya plan to redraw maritime boundaries in the Mediterranean as part of a new economic corridor. This has sparked strong protests from Greece, and has also drawn the European Union into the conflict.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Guinea-Bissau remain trapped in political chaos?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e6f64f8d93b2f8b7f01d44f7aa709a3ff7aa81805564a1764d164e522ba6f36</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-guinea-bissau-remain-trapped-in-political-chaos/a-79734069--662f4c5402cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-guinea-bissau-remain-trapped-in-political-chaos/a-79734069?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections scheduled for December 6 in Guinea-Bissau have been postponed indefinitely. No new date has been set, leaving the country's return to civilian rule uncertain.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4027f39c77701bf285de416f545548c09447fdcea618ee29bea25b3f114e0186</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz calls for unity at CSU party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0c7768df9d035532587e716ab4537e8b72d8fd560cbc2c13aad2cde408b2128</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-unity-at-csu-party-conference/live-79749353--718b2e6284ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-unity-at-csu-party-conference/live-79749353?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With his coalition under pressure, Merz delivered an address at the close of the CSU conference in Munich. Meanwhile, fire has largely destroyed Hitler's former Eagle's Nest retreat. DW has more</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travels to Chinese border city via newly opened bridge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f07483db17a53d52a947f27505f67a270abe933636037ecace0f9cd15c10e8ad</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T07:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-leader-kim-jong-un-travels-to-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580--1461c3f06f45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-leader-kim-jong-un-travels-to-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travelled to China’s border city of Dandong via a newly opened bridge linking the two countries, where he met a senior Chinese official.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Clashes break out as protests go nationwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fefbc86fddbbe2c224f8e00d33ed2a2cf2b718f926877f7d191da5ea3e77ec29</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T06:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-clashes-break-out-as-protests-go-nationwide/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police and elite security forces were out in force in French cities as tens of thousands participated in protests on Saturday. The situation turned tense toward the end of protests in several cities, including Paris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Russia's arrest of Japanese journalist is the latest sign of deteriorating ties between the countries.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c33cbdb9bdeb41241f2c7a00bc60933b3da1d7dc36d9e1f906ec322b7a689844</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-coun/a-79742995--e6439f04b25d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-countries/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Typhoon Champi leaves 1 dead, over 500 injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:787ee030b0d6ff4999563bab9adf6bf72ac77f51d030a78fdca231b5438efaad</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221--2c62bf3b9cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After killing one person and causing major disruptions in Taiwan, Typhoon Champi is now headed towards China.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Andhra, Odisha brace for severe storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e27f001ebf201bc9e768621446dbed5a50882f36a4ff379190d4db801a937dc0</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:58:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T04:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-andhra-odisha-brace-for-severe-storm/live-79748098--28c155f98f4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-andhra-odisha-brace-for-severe-storm/live-79748098?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The weather department warned that a depression over the Bay of Bengal could escalate into a very severe cyclonic storm before crossing the Andhra Pradesh 