e>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543b318cf608ba0e336736e6a9c40514a7fadae37105f49311b4870b81162a90</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d71fe3f095c11fe8a44b187dd5964ec3a0afa78c6fe0349d8d9af2899a78086</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Labor Minister Bärbel Bas has stepped down, citing her need to grieve a loved one and leave behind the harsh realities of government. So how did German politics get so heated?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cda98b266b8cd1431773d05504362f84a2b1480d636ede22406ccea5ee835df3</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><lin