and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:215149488582d30ce9a491d8c48b614c46c5dd61ee2d901b1c71ff5c86b7cb4e</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97904dfaa4bf8b1e1a38d5b60a8d487215936176644386adeae7cfa0c28b494b</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino is a 'postcard from the future' — and could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4560c5665c22c6ceee76c1033a06c689b295038438190401876976b21d2a3adb</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945--e1a2336874a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current El Nino could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths. Researchers warn it offers a glimpse of temperatures that may become normal within 20 years.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>South Park satirist pushes for accountability in Cornell gang-rape lawsuit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27ab0938deb5ab5057c53a82e19d21ae5acc3d4829d9da4149eb1a095719da93</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382--e2bb4e991ce2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Writer Toby Morton is using a new website to amplify allegations in a high-profile sexual assault lawsuit involving seven Cornell students. The reopening of the case is causing an outcry on social media.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6787f87035fd567baf07d101deb587be8edadd8772eeb003295dc6b51dd91ec2</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Spain grows fruit and vegetables for Europe, but it's running out of water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da120504125940a2f808805887734780628842d7b5687dfea7f8219e45372a18</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905--7611f918b844.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's southern coast produces up to 25% of Europe's fruit and vegetables. But amid intensive farming, climate change and illegal wells, the water it takes to grow them is drying up.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>What do Manchester City's charges mean for German football?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32294c273c21fdb7c40af21500d79b66bca8d1e4e758bf8a67ffe4537007089e</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412--ba8ebfa60874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manchester City have reportedly been found guilty of major financial rule breaches. What does this mean for German football?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Diesel prices are surging putting further pressure on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4e074813b39962da095dec7af1e9ef472fdde8fdb23ef2c5611cfae4f29a867</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992--edb37306aa00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trucks, farms and industry are powered with diesel. Now prices are soaring due to refinery disruptions, supply shortages and geopolitical tensions. A potential US export ban could make Europe's diesel crunch even worse.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Will Jürgen Klopp's charisma be enough for Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0acf3a3cacca84e01423929cf7c5c2909532fa22da7eed32841a6698ca9fae</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-j_rgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266--fed309f9f1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-jürgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After defeat to Greece, Jürgen Klopp faces the first real test of his tenure as coach of Germany's national men's football team. Can his charisma alone push this group forward?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland beat Israel 3-0 in Nations League match overshadowed by political controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1267253d3137e9b227f61790d66bbdb0289683cb969ce5ab274b45a43ea75c47</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254--ac737f0c12b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ireland easily beat Israel in a Nations League fixture that 24 hours earlier appeared in doubt. One Irish player pulled out of the match to express his opposition to Israel's actions in the Gaza Strip.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What would Francis of Assisi make of his fame today?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73b8422c9fd2aa9dc7307a38e852c90cdad8e4db86dbbd5fa4ae56b0cfead0e2</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T06:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-francis-of-assisi-make-of-his-fame-today/a-79346151--db42471ab90e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-francis-of-assisi-make-of-his-fame-today/a-79346151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Catholic saint renounced wealth and fame to become a mendicant friar. Yet throughout history, his teachings and life have inspired popes, Dante and even Mussolini.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ddcde74c82a73dbf75da70d13400fd2c98135f0b880a28968647d0a7322ab85</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
